g World  War two and he was on Okinawa he was the  only black officer walked in Samuel  Barnes he was one of the first black  officers in the United States Navy every  white officer in the club walked out  except one Steve Belichick and he'd  befriended the man and Barnes's family  that the Belichick name means a great  deal to them for that reason they were  roommates for short period of time and I  think I think that really shaped Bill I  think he grew up in a household that was  way ahead of its time and race relations  in this country and that  credit to his father his mother and I  think that's why when people wonder how  does Bill really inspire or connect with  the african-american athlete I think  it's because of his father and mother  and the way he was raised in that in  that home and that's one of the reasons  why I really opened the book with that  anecdote Congrats on the book good luck  with it and great to talk to you again  Ian thanks for joining us thank you Dan  appreciate it let's see an O'Connor ESPN  senior writer the book is Belichick the  making of the greatest football coach of  all time for more Dan Patrick show to  the audience channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]
 

